WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.470 align:start position:0%
 
you wanted the devil  well you got him the devil is in the  details and that doesn't ring more true  than for the effects in lucifer with six  seasons packed full of beautiful visuals  the vfx team had their hands full  creating this epic story the behind the  scenes will make you wonder how they  took something that looks so boring and  bare and turned it into the epic scenes  we see on screen they must have made a  deal with the devil to make the effects  look this good on such a tight schedule  and budget oh yeah  watch this  as the king of hell lucifer isn't your  ordinary fallen angel while he may  appear to be a handsome bachelor on the  outside on the inside lucifer hides a  devilish look we don't see it often but  every now and again we get a look at  lucifer's true complexion known to fans  as his devil face the first time we see  this is in the pilot episode of the  series we only get a glimpse for a few  seconds but it's enough to make out the  look  this is actually the only time the  effects department used makeup and  prosthetics to accomplish the look as  future iterations would be achieved with  cgi and there were multiple iterations  along the way season 1 and season 2 had  a smoother design with some folds and  cuts season 3 is where the look reached  its most well-known form with only  slight changes being made in the  following seasons actor tom ellis had  tracking dots painted on his face to  assist the vfx team in post-production  bridge what's going on here  the effects reference that was for when  we only saw the face but season 4  introduced us to lucifer's full devil  body including wings for this ellis wore  a full motion capture tracking suit  including a cap and of course the motion  dots on his face again we can say it was  worth it though as his devil appearance  looks incredible  one aspect of lucifer that's impossible  to miss are his giant wings they are cut  off in the first season but return in  the season two finale they were actually  brought back after amena deal lost his  wings strictly because the budget could  not sustain them we had him but we don't  think we can sustain the level  production and make these wings work the  creators decided they would rather  lucifer have wings and so amena deal  lost his although the writers did a  great job of making it part of his  character arc the wings were completely  cgi and took a lot of time to render but  they didn't require as much onset help  as you might think tom ellis didn't have  to wear any special tracking suit for  the wings in fact he wore his normal  suits and green tracking markers were  taped to the back simple right this  actually turned out to be a huge  headache for the crew the tape didn't  actually adhere all too well to the nice  suits and kept falling off this is a  bigger problem than one might think the  tape has to be put back on in the exact  same spot or else the vfx shot will be  imperfect let's look at a scene where  lucifer uses his wings in this scene  where lucifer is having a dream where  chloe is falling tom ellis is actually  on a green screen and the environment is  computer generated and in the season 3  finale when lucifer makes a grand  entrance to get revenge on kane  everything is cgi including lucifer  himself the scene transitions into a  live-action fight scene while keeping  the cg wings and it does so flawlessly  the devil has his ways of tricking us  the first wings we did  were supposed to be the last wings of  the show the process of creating the  angel wings for lucifer was anything but  straightforward to begin with they  weren't even sure if they were going to  be sustainable on their budget it's a  common thing that for budgetary reasons  not because of narrative reasons  someone's written or some aspect of a  show right now once they knew they were  going to be bringing back the wings  regularly they created big beautiful  feathers that had their own custom rake  for the vfx team to animate with there  were multiple elements to manipulate the  wing rig which controlled how the  overall wings moved and reacted and the  individual feathers which could be  transformed in multiple different ways  and some of the feathers they created  for lucifer were really big the ones on  the end of his wings are like as big as  his leg with so many detailed feathers  and animation rendering a single frame  took five to six hours he was like okay  yeah this is gonna work another giant  headache for the vfx department was the  scene in the season 3 finale where  lucifer shields and protects chloe with  his wings they had to create an entirely  new pipeline to create this scene and  just figuring out how to do it took them  a full month some new challenges they  faced included getting the feathers to  bend correctly and making them bleed  that's not the only unique aspect of our  favorite fallen angel just like the  wings lucifer's devil face also had to  undergo changes as the seasons  progressed a couple of the main things  the vfx team focused on tweaking were  his eyes and making his overall look  less smooth we just kind of take divots  out of him and make more gouges they did  all this work for the big reveal at the  end of the season 3 finale only for the  show to be cancelled right after luckily  it was brought back on netflix so we  could see more devil face and wings than  ever as netflix's budget allowed for  more vfx shots this included bringing  back the updated devil face this time  with a devil body and wings to go along  with it but the wings and face aren't  the only things that make lucifer  lucifer he is the ruler of hell after  all and can't be spending all of his  time on earth one of the most impressive  shots of the series comes at the end of  the season 4 finale when lucifer returns  to hell he presides over his kingdom  sitting high above the land in a giant  chair to create this scene they shot tom  ellis on a simplified version of the  chair on a raised stage and a green  screen background the behind the scenes  definitely isn't quite as epic as the  final shot but it shows how drastically  vfx can change the look of a scene  while we've been taking a look at the  grand expensive and in your face vfx  shots there are some special effects  sprinkled throughout the show that you  may not have even noticed when kane is  impaled during his fight with amena deal  despite going through him isn't there at  all it was completely added in post and  when lucifer finds out that pierce is  actually kane and stabs him the knife  blade is cgi actor tom welling was  holding a handle and feigning the action  of pulling the blade out of his chest  that scene in season 3 where lucifer  intimidates a murder suspect by dangling  him off a cliff real car with green  screen on the ground and the cliff  created digitally and who can forget  that fantastic dance sequence in season  4 where lucifer pulls a dirty dancing  and lifts dan in the air this was done  practically with wires which were  removed in post the result was an oddly  perfect sequence of the devil showing  everyone his incredible moves but that's  not all there are some scenes you would  never guess contain visual effects  during a scene at a ballerina recital  the entire audience was added separately  and when the car explodes next to  lucifer and chloe they replaced the  stunt doubles face with actress laura  germans even though it's only on screen  for a second it's the small attention to  details like these that help keep the  audience engaged in the show with them  none the wiser of the amazing work done  by the vfx team it's impressive what  these vfx artists are able to accomplish  with such little time and money they  pour their hard work into these effects  and the results speak for themselves the  amount of work they do with the amount  of limitations they have is nothing  short of spectacular from angels to  devils the effects in lucifer have only  continued to improve throughout the  seasons which effect do you think was  most impressive

